+++ b/docs/NATIVE-ROTATION-ABORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Native refusal and ledger abort contract
+
+This source implementation adds `rotation_native_abort` to the isolated TaskLedger. It is not yet connected to the host supervisor or exposed through the daemon/MCP adapter. Native refusal publication and host file/process verification are prerequisites for that connection.
+
+## Required native record
+
+An immutable native refusal record has exactly these fields:
+
+- `v`: integer 1
+- `state`: `refused`
+- `operation_id`: the original rotation UUID
+- `claim_id`: the host claim UUID
+- `reservation_id`: the original native reservation UUID
+- `capsule_sha256`: the exact capsule digest
+- `source`: native runtime/thread/turn/rollout identity and unsigned integer admission generation
+- `process_id`: the original enrolled provider PID
+
+The host must verify the actual private native file, its owner/process incarnation and conflicts with native lifecycle records. JSON validation alone establishes no cancellation or native authority. A missing journal, elapsed lease, timeout or source-retained response is insufficient.
+
+## Ledger transaction
+
+The request contains exactly `v, session_id, epoch, claim_id, token, host_claim_id, request_sha256, receipt`. Claim/token identity, durable intent digest and the entire native refusal must match. Registration or ACK excludes abort. The original source remains Relay-owned Codex in the same working directory at first acceptance.
+
+Acceptance writes `abort`, closes the claim and marks the intent `aborted` in one WAL transaction. The same positive sequence binds all three records. It performs no native action and sets `lifecycle_performed=false`. Expired claims may be resolved by verified refusal, while expiry itself cannot resolve them.
+
+Exact retry returns the saved abort without a WAL write or changing a newer active epoch. Historical status preserves all evidence. Default status reports availability only when the complete abort history is internally consistent. A fresh operation needs a new UUID and fresh admission.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
